                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Preventive Maintenance Manual\n3. Maintenance levels\nAtlas uses two scheduled maintenance levels and one corrective level.\nPM-1, Performed by = Machine operator. PM-1, What it is = Daily or weekly inspection and lubrication on the round sheet. PM-1, Recorded = Paper round sheet, kept 12 months. PM-2, Performed by = Maintenance technician. PM-2, What it is = Full preventive service to the task list for the machine type. PM-2, Recorded = CMMS event, event type planned, task code PM-2. Corrective (CM), Performed by = Maintenance technician. Corrective (CM), What it is = Repair after a failure or a condition alarm. Corrective (CM), Recorded = CMMS event, event type unplanned, task code CM, with a failure code\nPM-1 is not entered in the CMMS. Only PM-2 services and corrective repairs appear in the maintenance event history.",
