                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Preventive Maintenance Manual\n6. Condition-based triggers\nSensors on every machine record daily vibration (average velocity in mm/s RMS), maximum temperature and alarm counts. A condition trigger can bring a PM-2 forward or start a corrective inspection before the interval in Table 1 is reached. Table 2 gives the levels for each machine type.\nCNC Mill, Vibration warning (mm/s) = 3.0. CNC Mill, Vibration alarm (mm/s) = 4.0. CNC Mill, Max temperature warning (C) = 60. CNC Mill, Max temperature alarm (C) = 70. CNC Lathe, Vibration warning (mm/s) = 3.5. CNC Lathe, Vibration alarm (mm/s) = 4.5. CNC Lathe, Max temperature warning (C) = 62. CNC Lathe, Max temperature alarm (C) = 72. Hydraulic Press, Vibration warning (mm/s) = 4.0. Hydraulic Press, Vibration alarm (mm/s) = 5.0. Hydraulic Press, Max temperature warning (C) = 62. Hydraulic Press, Max temperature alarm (C) = 70. Robot Cell, Vibration warning (mm/s) = 2.5. Robot Cell, Vibration alarm (mm/s) = 3.5. Robot Cell, Max temperature warning (C) = 55. Robot Cell, Max temperature alarm (C) = 65. Surface Grinder, Vibration warning (mm/s) = 2.5. Surface Grinder, Vibration alarm (mm/s) = 3.5. Surface Grinder, Max temperature warning (C) = 58. Surface Grinder, Max temperature alarm (C) = 68\nTable 2. Vibration and temperature warning and alarm levels by machine type.",
